# KB maintenance with every app update

The user requires TMA-Padlock to follow the same ongoing KB maintenance standard
as TMApps Launcher. Treat relevant documentation as part of completing an update.

- Review changes for effects on setup, features, settings, supported platforms,
  performance, privacy and troubleshooting. Update relevant existing articles;
  add a new article when a distinct topic needs its own guide.
- Preserve existing KB identifiers and reference conventions. If none exist, use
  `Padlock-KB1`, `Padlock-KB2`, and so on. Append new numbers after the highest
  existing number; never reuse or renumber an existing article.
- Use the app's existing KB content source. If no KB exists, establish its first
  guides with the next relevant feature update. Keep any in-app help and Word
  library consistent; do not add unrelated product features just to apply this rule.
- Include relevant real screenshots where they help explain the instructions.
  Refresh captures when affected UI changes. Use sanitized example data and
  captions. Never capture real passwords, keys, tokens, recovery codes, vault
  contents, mail, private projects or other sensitive user information.
- Maintain the app's KB Library Word document at its established path, or use
  `docs/KB Library.docx` when creating it. Follow the documents skill for artifact
  authoring. Keep release/date metadata accurate and preserve a reproducible
  generator where one exists.
- Make index entries and all KB references clickable buttons linking to the
  relevant article section. Include Back to index navigation. Preserve stable
  bookmarks and validate every target, including new articles.
- Render and visually inspect every page before publishing a changed Word
  document. Verify screenshot readability, captions, page breaks and navigation.
- Include updated KB sources, screenshots and the reviewed Word document in
  the relevant app update on `TMA-Padlock`. Follow this app's existing release
  policy; this requirement alone does not authorize a version bump or release.
  When attaching the document to a shared GitHub release, use an app-specific
  asset name so it cannot replace the launcher or another app's KB Library.
- Document implemented, verified behaviour and current platform limitations.
  Clearly label prepared or unavailable features. If an update has no relevant
  user-facing KB impact, record that assessment rather than inventing an article.

## Suite library requirements (23 October 2026)

Publish docs/(App Name) KB Library.docx with app name, approved logo and app colours
on every page. Retain legacy KB Library.docx links until consumers are migrated.
Link the main-branch TMApps Master KB Library on page one once published; never
claim an unpublished document is available. Keep stable KB IDs, working index and
cross-reference links, setup, user guides, actual errors/resolutions and escalation.
Include explicit offline/online coverage. Use real sanitized screenshots. Render
and visually inspect every changed Word page before upload. Keep in-app Help,
optional KB search results, Wiki articles and the main KB registry aligned.
